    "title": "pandas.Series.list.len — pandas 3.1.0.dev0 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Series.list.len#\n\n- Series.list.len()[source]#\n- Return the length of each list in the Series. Computes the number of elements in each list entry. The result is a Series of integers with the same index as the original Series. \n  - Returns:\n    - pandas.Series\n    - The length of each list.\n See also \n  - `str.len`\n  - Python built-in function returning the length of an object.\n  - `Series.size`\n  - Returns the length of the Series.\n  - `StringMethods.len`\n  - Compute the length of each element in the Series/Index.\n Examples >>> import pyarrow as pa >>> s = pd.Series( ... [ ... [1, 2, 3], ... [3], ... ], ... dtype=pd.ArrowDtype(pa.list_(pa.int64())), ... ) >>> s.list.len() 0 3 1 1 dtype: int32[pyarrow]",
